- **How much to trust it.** We tested the method by forecasting 13 weeks ahead from 8 past starting points. It missed by {wape_reg}% on average, compared with {wape_naive}% for "same as last week." The stated 80% ranges captured {pi_cov}% of actual days.
- **The notice effect is measured, not assumed.** The September 2025 notice raised billing and cancellation calls {pn_lift}% on the day it went out. The extra volume halved about every {pn_hl} days, and calls ran {aht_lift}% longer for two weeks.

## Why act now

The center answered {sl_2025}% of calls within 60 seconds in 2025, against a goal of 80%, and {ab_2025}% of callers hung up. Volume grows about {trend}% a month, and the schedule has not kept pace.

## Worth exploring

Five separate queues each need their own buffer of idle agents. If one cross-trained team answered every queue, the same service level would need about {pooled_save} fewer FTE. A pilot cross-training billing and cancellations would test how much of that saving holds in practice.
